# __GAME__

A co-op game on [unified](https://github.com/FylmTM/godot-unified) (deterministic rollback netcode, Odin + Godot), started
from `uni init`: a copy of unified's `examples/minimal_3d`, where 1–4 players move capsules and throw balls up. Make it
yours from here, starting with the design below (a draft skeleton: the game's rules, before its code).

```
./uni test --suite all # the sim tests and the game under headless Godot (uni.cmd on Windows)
./uni run              # play, in a window
./uni headless -- synctest --ticks 600 --window 8 # the sim without Godot (-- help: every mode)
./uni help             # every command
```

- `simulation/__GAME__/`: the deterministic sim (unified/src/sim/README.md: f32 only, no pointers in the state):
  `game.odin` (the Game and its tick), `state.odin` (State), `input.odin` (Input and the commands), `events.odin`,
  a file per part of the rules (`players.odin`, `balls.odin`) and `script.odin` (the scripted players of tests and
  headless runs).
- `simulation/headless/`: the headless binary (offline runs, sync-tests, benchmarks).
- `simulation/extension/`: the GDExtension: the sim run by unified's Godot integration (unified/src/godot/README.md):
  `input.odin` turns Godot's input into an Input, `frame.odin` the state into views.
- `simulation/tests/`: the standard scenarios and the determinism lint (`suite_test.odin`, which says how to pin a
  reference run), and the game's own rule tests.
- `game/`: the Godot side: scenes, views (each with a UnifiedView marker, which the build indexes) and scripts.
  GDScript reads the sim; input and commands are the only way in.
- `tools/`: this game's CLI (unified's public commands, plus the game's own).
- `unified/`: unified, as a git submodule. Local paths (a Godot install, the EOS SDK) go in a git-ignored `.env`.
- `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/skills/`: for coding agents (`unified/docs/agent-guide.md`).

## What to take from where

A game stays this shape: no menus or settings, one scene that starts a session. unified's example games
(`unified/examples/`) show the rest; survivor's, drift's and friendslop's menus, settings and HUD panels (`game/app/`,
`game/ui/`) are their own, not a template:

- **Playing together:** the session's flags and `uni coop`. Direct (LAN) works as is (`--host-port`, `--join`,
  `uni coop --lan`); online (EOS lobbies and P2P: `--host-online`, `--join-code`) once the game passes
  `eos.lobby({})` to `godot.init` and `lobbies` to `modes.run` (drift's extension, survivor's headless main).
- **A physics World on a level with markers:** friendslop (3D: characters, joints, sensors), drift (2D on a plane).
- **Level changes:** friendslop (`Game.levels`, a travel command, `physics.level_change`, the session's `level_root`).
- **Several local players on one machine:** drift (a pad joins with Start; the extension's `sample_input` reads each
  local player's device).
- **A Setup, a Profile and a save:** survivor (the difficulty and the host's record through the Setup, a role per
  player in the Profile, the record on the match-over panel).
- **Opening a running game to friends:** friendslop's pause menu (online when the build has online play, else on the
  LAN).
- **Pausing:** the co-op pause here (a `sim.Clock` and a command, as state); the single-player pause,
  `UnifiedSession.paused`, in the other games' pause menus.
- **Tables, handles, a view per entity, rule tests on `headless.Run`:** drift.
- **A population, a benchmark with `bench_prepare`, keyed rolls, a tuning variant:** survivor, with dev commands,
  timing zones, debug draws, a `sim.Grid`, `sim.due` and a roll its HUD peeks.
- **How a view is shown:** friendslop (a script-posed view, `Glue.view_policy`: the held item at the hand), drift and
  friendslop (a teleported body's view snaps: `physics.body_warp`), survivor (a warp epoch of its own for a body made
  again).
- **Shown by no game** (the declaration's doc comment says how): `Appear.Verified` and `Glue.multi_policy`,
  `sim.Queue`, `sim.Bits`, dmath's trig, `Game.predict_input`, `Game.input_delay_min_ticks`.
